1
00:00:04,700 --> 00:00:11,667
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

2
00:00:31,500 --> 00:00:32,567
[TIRES SCREECHING]

3
00:00:33,867 --> 00:00:34,800
[ENGINE REVVING]

4
00:00:39,833 --> 00:00:41,033
[TIRES SCREECH]

5
00:00:42,033 --> 00:00:43,700
[ENGINES REVVING]

6
00:00:43,833 --> 00:00:44,833
[TRUCK HORN BLARES]

7
00:00:44,967 --> 00:00:46,000
[LOUD CRASH]

8
00:00:46,667 --> 00:00:48,600
[TIRES SCREECHING]

9
00:00:49,867 --> 00:00:50,933
<i>- Stop!
- [GUNSHOT]</i>

10
00:00:52,333 --> 00:00:53,300
[FIREWORKS EXPLODING]

11
00:00:53,433 --> 00:00:55,200
- [ENGINES REVVING]
- [BUS HORN HONKS]

12
00:00:56,433 --> 00:00:57,900
[GLASS SHATTERING]

13
00:00:58,033 --> 00:01:00,100
- [TIRES SCREECHING]
- [LOUD CRASH]

14
00:01:00,833 --> 00:01:03,100
[ENGINES REVVING]

15
00:01:04,733 --> 00:01:06,200
[TIRES SCREECHING]

16
00:01:07,100 --> 00:01:09,133
[TIRES SCREECHING]

17
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:11,467
- [GUNSHOT]
- [TIRES SCREECHING]

18
00:01:11,600 --> 00:01:12,733
- [TRUCK HORN BLARES]
- [LOUD CRASH]

19
00:01:12,867 --> 00:01:14,633
[TIRES SCREECHING]

20
00:01:19,600 --> 00:01:21,733
<i> I didn't sign any papers</i>

21
00:01:21,867 --> 00:01:23,433
<i>saying we'd request
extra manpower from the NLEA.</i>

22
00:01:23,567 --> 00:01:24,467
<i> You can all leave now.</i>

23
00:01:24,600 --> 00:01:27,667
<i>You shouldn't have left.
Follow the convoy.</i>

24
00:01:30,167 --> 00:01:31,533
<i> Hurry! Let's lock him up!</i>

25
00:01:31,667 --> 00:01:33,133
<i> If you're doing everything,</i>

26
00:01:33,267 --> 00:01:34,900
<i>then you should've found Sam
by now!</i>

27
00:01:35,033 --> 00:01:37,067
<i>It's an embarrassment
that my own daughter</i>

28
00:01:37,200 --> 00:01:38,767
<i> is a victim of a crime!</i>

29
00:01:38,900 --> 00:01:39,867
<i> Here are the materials.</i>

30
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:41,733
<i>- Your roof's too old.
- Be careful!</i>

31
00:01:41,900 --> 00:01:43,067
<i> All of them seem kind.</i>

32
00:01:43,200 --> 00:01:44,300
<i> They're good at pretending.</i>

33
00:01:44,433 --> 00:01:47,067
<i>But I'm the one
making a fool out of them.</i>

34
00:01:47,200 --> 00:01:48,967
<i>Maybe it's better
that she stays here inside.</i>

35
00:01:49,100 --> 00:01:50,233
<i> Let her be.</i>

36
00:01:50,367 --> 00:01:52,667
She might think we're caging her
<i> inside this house.</i>

37
00:01:52,800 --> 00:01:55,467
<i>- Is this Gabo's motorcycle?
- No, but he used it.</i>

38
00:01:55,600 --> 00:01:57,967
<i>Does Gabo use this
for illegal activities?</i>

39
00:01:58,100 --> 00:01:59,400
<i> Gabo has changed his ways.</i>

40
00:01:59,533 --> 00:02:02,067
<i>But it's like
he attracts misfortune.</i>

41
00:02:04,967 --> 00:02:05,833
[KNOCKS ON DOOR]

42
00:02:05,967 --> 00:02:07,167
- Sir?
- Yes?

43
00:02:07,300 --> 00:02:10,200
Sir, there was trouble
during the transfer!

44
00:02:10,333 --> 00:02:14,533
- Trouble? What happened?
- Victor almost escaped!

45
00:02:14,700 --> 00:02:18,700
The Zafras prepared
for Victor's transfer!

46
00:02:18,833 --> 00:02:23,200
How did the Zafras find out
about Tiger's transfer?!

47
00:02:24,067 --> 00:02:25,167
I don't know, sir.

48
00:02:26,067 --> 00:02:27,933
The team. Are they safe?

49
00:02:28,567 --> 00:02:29,767
Team Alpha is alive.

50
00:02:30,600 --> 00:02:31,967
However, Team Charlie...

51
00:02:33,333 --> 00:02:34,533
...did not survive.

52
00:02:35,767 --> 00:02:36,833
- Here.
- [SMACKS HANDS]

53
00:02:37,733 --> 00:02:39,500
That's your 6th cup of coffee.

54
00:02:40,533 --> 00:02:43,000
It's fine. Caffeine doesn't work
on me anymore.

55
00:02:44,600 --> 00:02:45,600
Tastes weird.

56
00:02:46,433 --> 00:02:47,367
Oh.

57
00:02:49,567 --> 00:02:51,267
So, is it done?

58
00:02:53,100 --> 00:02:54,233
[GROANING]

59
00:02:54,367 --> 00:02:56,800
- What happened?
- Sir, when we arrived,

60
00:02:56,933 --> 00:03:00,133
the NCIA and the armed men
were already fighting.

61
00:03:01,067 --> 00:03:02,767
So? Were the NCIA people killed?

62
00:03:02,900 --> 00:03:06,867
A lot of them did, sir,
and the detainee almost escaped.

63
00:03:07,000 --> 00:03:08,800
But the NCIA caught him back.

64
00:03:10,100 --> 00:03:12,433
H-How many of us were killed?

65
00:03:12,567 --> 00:03:14,633
There are some.
Others are wounded.

66
00:03:14,767 --> 00:03:18,667
Luckily, we arrived just in time
to fight those armed men.

67
00:03:20,133 --> 00:03:21,200
Okay.

68
00:03:21,367 --> 00:03:23,167
We're the heroes here.
You understand?

69
00:03:23,300 --> 00:03:24,800
- Yes, sir.
- Tell it to our troops.

70
00:03:24,933 --> 00:03:26,467
We're the heroes, okay?

71
00:03:26,600 --> 00:03:28,067
- Tend to your wounds.
- Yes, sir.

72
00:03:31,100 --> 00:03:32,067
Us, sir?

73
00:03:32,667 --> 00:03:35,167
We weren't part of--

74
00:03:35,300 --> 00:03:36,633
- Did we go there?
- Hey.

75
00:03:37,300 --> 00:03:39,400
We saved the NCIA.

76
00:03:40,000 --> 00:03:42,600
NLEA are the heroes here.
Do you understand?

77
00:03:44,667 --> 00:03:46,267
Sir needs to know this.

78
00:03:49,067 --> 00:03:50,033
[SIGHS]

79
00:03:50,600 --> 00:03:51,900
[PHONE RINGING]

80
00:03:52,567 --> 00:03:54,600
- [PHONE RINGING]
- [SIGHS]

81
00:03:57,133 --> 00:03:58,867
- Domingo.
- General Jacinto.

82
00:03:59,000 --> 00:03:59,867
What's the news?

83
00:04:00,000 --> 00:04:01,833
[DOMINGO] Victor Zafra is now

84
00:04:01,967 --> 00:04:04,967
in a maximum security facility.
Mission accomplished, General.

85
00:04:05,100 --> 00:04:07,900
Have you forgotten that
my daughter is still missing?

86
00:04:08,033 --> 00:04:09,533
Until you find her...

87
00:04:10,267 --> 00:04:11,633
You can't rest.

88
00:04:12,567 --> 00:04:14,300
[LINE DROPS]

89
00:04:15,533 --> 00:04:22,533
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

90
00:04:24,767 --> 00:04:26,867
Gloria! Come on,
let's go inside.

91
00:04:27,000 --> 00:04:28,467
- Come on, dear.
- [SAM] Alright.

92
00:04:28,633 --> 00:04:29,633
You even bought vegetables.

93
00:04:29,767 --> 00:04:31,933
Oh, no.
Someone just gave it to me.

94
00:04:33,000 --> 00:04:34,033
[ROOF CLANGING]

95
00:04:34,167 --> 00:04:35,767
Ahh!

96
00:04:35,900 --> 00:04:36,833
Hey!

97
00:04:37,533 --> 00:04:38,667
[BODY THUDS]

98
00:04:39,800 --> 00:04:41,367
Badong! Badong!

99
00:04:41,500 --> 00:04:43,400
- Help!
- [ELTON] Badong, here it is.

100
00:04:43,533 --> 00:04:45,400
Wake up! E-Elton!

101
00:04:45,533 --> 00:04:47,867
- What happened to Badong?!
- He fell off the roof!

102
00:04:48,000 --> 00:04:50,733
- Huh?!
- Badong, Badong! Wake up!

103
00:04:51,267 --> 00:04:53,167
- Help!
- He's unconscious!

104
00:04:53,300 --> 00:04:54,767
I'll call Rudy!

105
00:04:54,900 --> 00:04:57,000
- Rudy!
- Oh?

106
00:04:57,133 --> 00:04:58,833
Badong fell off the roof.

107
00:04:58,967 --> 00:04:59,900
- What?!
- What?!

108
00:05:00,033 --> 00:05:01,433
- [ELTON] He's unconscious!
- [RUDY] Let's go!

109
00:05:01,600 --> 00:05:04,200
I told you
that roof's too fragile!

110
00:05:04,333 --> 00:05:11,233
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

111
00:05:19,367 --> 00:05:22,300
- Badong!
- He fell off the roof!

112
00:05:22,433 --> 00:05:24,033
- Badong!
- Help carry him.

113
00:05:24,167 --> 00:05:28,533
[DIDAY] Carry him, hurry!
Take him to the hospital!

114
00:05:28,667 --> 00:05:31,300
Wait, wait!
Don't carry him like that.

115
00:05:31,433 --> 00:05:32,900
- [NEIGHBOR] Let go, let go.
- Not like that.

116
00:05:33,033 --> 00:05:35,800
His injury will get worse.
Put him down gently.

117
00:05:35,967 --> 00:05:37,133
Move aside for a second.

118
00:05:39,467 --> 00:05:40,467
- [SAM GRUNTS]
- Gloria.

119
00:05:44,300 --> 00:05:45,600
[SAM] His pulse is fine.

120
00:05:46,100 --> 00:05:47,333
He needs to lay down
on something.

121
00:05:47,467 --> 00:05:48,900
- Like a plank.
- Here, here.

122
00:05:49,033 --> 00:05:50,267
[OVERLAPPING CHATTER]

123
00:05:53,767 --> 00:05:54,800
[DANTE] Here, here.

124
00:05:54,933 --> 00:05:56,900
[SAM] Alright, everyone, listen.

125
00:05:57,033 --> 00:05:59,667
I'm going to count to three.
When I say roll,

126
00:05:59,800 --> 00:06:02,433
we'll gently turn him
to his side.

127
00:06:02,567 --> 00:06:04,733
I'll count again,
we'll lay him down,

128
00:06:04,867 --> 00:06:06,333
and we'll slide
this wood underneath.

129
00:06:06,467 --> 00:06:07,433
- Understood?
- Yes.

130
00:06:07,600 --> 00:06:09,167
You'll have to support his head.

131
00:06:09,300 --> 00:06:11,000
- Alright, alright.
- Okay?

132
00:06:11,133 --> 00:06:13,300
One, two, three, roll.

133
00:06:13,433 --> 00:06:14,533
- Roll, roll, roll, roll.
- Slide.

134
00:06:14,667 --> 00:06:17,167
- Okay, okay, okay.
- Alright. Lay him down.

135
00:06:17,300 --> 00:06:20,067
- There.
- Slowly. Okay.

136
00:06:20,200 --> 00:06:21,567
[NEIGHBOR] One, two, three.

137
00:06:22,267 --> 00:06:23,500
Put his head in front.

138
00:06:23,633 --> 00:06:25,933
- His head, his head.
- His head.

139
00:06:26,067 --> 00:06:27,233
All good? Then let's go!

140
00:06:27,367 --> 00:06:29,000
- I can't believe this.
- Did you warn him?

141
00:06:29,133 --> 00:06:30,100
- Careful!
- Look out!

142
00:06:30,233 --> 00:06:31,767
- Come on!
- I told Badong to be careful!

143
00:06:31,900 --> 00:06:33,467
- Hurry!
- But he didn't listen!

144
00:06:33,600 --> 00:06:35,200
And now look at what happened!

145
00:06:35,967 --> 00:06:37,000
He got into an accident!

146
00:06:37,133 --> 00:06:38,133
[SAM] Be careful now!

147
00:06:38,267 --> 00:06:39,533
[INDISTINCT CROWD CHATTER]

148
00:06:39,667 --> 00:06:41,400
- What happened to Badong?
- He fell!

149
00:06:41,567 --> 00:06:44,033
- Make way, make way!
- Step aside, please!

150
00:06:44,267 --> 00:06:45,233
[GABO] Hey, what's wrong?

151
00:06:45,367 --> 00:06:47,233
[MAMENG]
Badong fell from the roof!

152
00:06:47,367 --> 00:06:48,633
We're taking him
to the hospital.

153
00:06:48,967 --> 00:06:50,733
Wha-- No! It's dangerous!

154
00:06:51,100 --> 00:06:52,033
Uh...

155
00:06:52,167 --> 00:06:53,133
Mister Elton!

156
00:06:53,267 --> 00:06:54,633
- Bring him to the hospital!
- [ELTON] Yes, Gabo!

157
00:06:54,767 --> 00:06:56,867
- Leave him to us! Let's go!
- Go on, hurry!

158
00:06:57,000 --> 00:06:58,267
- Go with him!
- Excuse me!

159
00:06:58,400 --> 00:07:00,167
- Move aside!
- Stay by his side!

160
00:07:00,300 --> 00:07:01,833
- Poor guy!
- Carry him!

161
00:07:01,967 --> 00:07:04,167
Come on, get inside.
It's not safe!

162
00:07:04,300 --> 00:07:05,933
- Why isn't it safe?
- We're in danger!

163
00:07:06,067 --> 00:07:07,033
[RUDY] Let's go, quickly!

164
00:07:07,167 --> 00:07:11,033
[GLOOMY MUSIC PLAYING]

165
00:07:11,167 --> 00:07:12,833
[SAM] What exactly is dangerous?

166
00:07:12,967 --> 00:07:16,333
[MAMENG] Right. Gabo, what
do you mean it's not safe?

167
00:07:16,967 --> 00:07:18,000
[GABO] Well...

168
00:07:18,133 --> 00:07:19,033
Nothing, Auntie.

169
00:07:19,167 --> 00:07:21,333
I was just surprised
to find Gloria outside.

170
00:07:21,467 --> 00:07:23,833
You know how dangerous
our neighborhood is.

171
00:07:23,967 --> 00:07:26,000
There are so many
nosy people around.

172
00:07:26,133 --> 00:07:28,500
They'll surely make her
the center of gossip.

173
00:07:28,633 --> 00:07:30,700
That's why it's risky
for Gloria.

174
00:07:30,833 --> 00:07:32,400
[DANTE] I thought it was
something serious.

175
00:07:32,533 --> 00:07:33,700
No, that's it, Uncle.

176
00:07:33,967 --> 00:07:35,600
By the way, Pa...

177
00:07:35,733 --> 00:07:40,400
Here's the snack you asked
me to get for Mister Badong.

178
00:07:40,533 --> 00:07:42,300
- So what now?
- [DANTE] Oh no...

179
00:07:42,433 --> 00:07:44,200
Badong was rushed
to the hospital.

180
00:07:44,333 --> 00:07:46,833
[MAMENG] Gosh, I just hope
he wasn't badly hurt.

181
00:07:46,967 --> 00:07:49,933
- I feel bad for him.
- Oh, it's nothing.

182
00:07:50,400 --> 00:07:51,767
A simple massage will
take care of it.

183
00:07:51,900 --> 00:07:53,033
[MAMENG] Just a massage?

184
00:07:53,167 --> 00:07:56,733
The guy was knocked out
and had a head wound.

185
00:07:56,867 --> 00:07:58,267
- Well, it's partly his fault.
- Come on.

186
00:07:58,400 --> 00:07:59,467
[GABO CHUCKLES SOFTLY]

187
00:08:00,300 --> 00:08:02,933
Love, I bought you some...

188
00:08:03,067 --> 00:08:04,100
<i> pagpag</i> (scavenged leftovers).

189
00:08:04,933 --> 00:08:06,100
- [CHUCKLES AWKWARDLY]
- [PLAYFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

190
00:08:06,233 --> 00:08:07,333
What's pagpag?

191
00:08:07,467 --> 00:08:10,433
Oh, that's been
Gabo's favorite food

192
00:08:10,567 --> 00:08:12,133
since he was a little boy.

193
00:08:12,267 --> 00:08:13,233
[GABO] That's true, Love.

194
00:08:13,367 --> 00:08:15,567
I've loved eating it
since I was a kid.

195
00:08:15,700 --> 00:08:18,333
I could eat it every single day.

196
00:08:18,467 --> 00:08:19,367
So...

197
00:08:19,500 --> 00:08:21,033
I was hoping
you could taste this.

198
00:08:21,300 --> 00:08:22,500
It's really delicious.

199
00:08:23,033 --> 00:08:26,000
Later at dinner,
this will be our meal.

200
00:08:27,000 --> 00:08:27,900
- Auntie?
- Hmm?

201
00:08:28,033 --> 00:08:30,400
- This will be our dinner.
- Of course.

202
00:08:30,533 --> 00:08:31,933
I'll just cook some rice.

203
00:08:32,067 --> 00:08:33,267
- [PLAYFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]
- [CHUCKLES SOFTLY]

204
00:08:33,400 --> 00:08:34,267
Pa.

205
00:08:34,400 --> 00:08:36,367
- [RUDY] Hmm?
- Look...

206
00:08:36,500 --> 00:08:38,400
I bought you something too.

207
00:08:38,533 --> 00:08:39,367
What?

208
00:08:39,500 --> 00:08:40,667
Take a look.

209
00:08:40,800 --> 00:08:42,167
Oh, son, you really went
out of your way.

210
00:08:42,300 --> 00:08:44,067
Well, I remembered something.

211
00:08:44,500 --> 00:08:46,367
Isn't it your birthday tomorrow?

212
00:08:46,500 --> 00:08:47,567
- [DANTE] Ooh.
- That's why...

213
00:08:47,700 --> 00:08:48,967
I bought you some clothes

214
00:08:49,100 --> 00:08:51,200
so you'll look
super handsome tomorrow.

215
00:08:51,333 --> 00:08:52,867
- You didn't have to, son.
- [DANTE] Happy birthday.

216
00:08:53,000 --> 00:08:54,200
It's no big deal, Pa.

217
00:08:54,767 --> 00:08:56,367
Uh... Pa?

218
00:08:56,500 --> 00:08:57,633
[MELLOW MUSIC PLAYING]

219
00:08:57,767 --> 00:09:00,133
Can we talk in the kitchen
for a while?

220
00:09:00,267 --> 00:09:01,700
I just have something to say.

221
00:09:01,833 --> 00:09:03,300
Sure thing. Let's go over there.

222
00:09:04,233 --> 00:09:05,400
[MAMENG] Let me sit down.

223
00:09:05,533 --> 00:09:06,600
Love, we'll just talk.

224
00:09:06,733 --> 00:09:08,800
- [MAMENG] That was exhausting.
- [DANTE EXHALES]

225
00:09:09,567 --> 00:09:10,633
- Here we go.
- My goodness.

226
00:09:10,767 --> 00:09:11,800
Sit down, dear.

227
00:09:12,300 --> 00:09:13,267
[CHAIR RATTLES]

228
00:09:15,033 --> 00:09:15,967
What is it, son?

229
00:09:16,100 --> 00:09:17,367
[MAMENG] Gosh, today was...

230
00:09:18,067 --> 00:09:19,000
Pa.

231
00:09:19,133 --> 00:09:21,767
That thing I said earlier
was dangerous...

232
00:09:22,200 --> 00:09:23,267
It's true.

233
00:09:23,400 --> 00:09:24,600
[UNSETTLING MUSIC PLAYING]

234
00:09:24,733 --> 00:09:27,400
I saw the men who were
looking for her last night.

235
00:09:27,567 --> 00:09:28,800
They were circling
the basketball court.

236
00:09:28,933 --> 00:09:30,467
I saw them
while I was buying food.

237
00:09:30,833 --> 00:09:33,100
Oh no. They're still here?

238
00:09:33,233 --> 00:09:36,500
Gloria is still in danger.

239
00:09:38,767 --> 00:09:40,033
[DANTE] You know, Gloria,

240
00:09:40,167 --> 00:09:41,467
I was really surprised by you.

241
00:09:41,600 --> 00:09:42,833
You impressed me.

242
00:09:42,967 --> 00:09:46,533
You know exactly what to do
in case of emergencies.

243
00:09:46,667 --> 00:09:48,100
[MAMENG] Same here, Gloria.

244
00:09:48,233 --> 00:09:49,900
How did you know all that?

245
00:09:50,033 --> 00:09:52,067
[UNSETTLING MUSIC CONTINUES]

246
00:09:52,200 --> 00:09:53,300
Uh...
[CHUCKLES AWKWARDLY]

247
00:09:53,600 --> 00:09:55,033
[STAMMERS]
Oh, I'm not really sure.

248
00:09:55,167 --> 00:09:56,100
It just...

249
00:09:56,233 --> 00:09:58,400
It just popped into my head.

250
00:09:58,533 --> 00:10:00,833
[MAMENG] Maybe your memories
are starting to come back.

251
00:10:02,267 --> 00:10:03,267
[CHUCKLES AWKWARDLY]

252
00:10:03,400 --> 00:10:05,300
I hope so. Honestly...

253
00:10:06,433 --> 00:10:08,667
I feel bad for Gabo.

254
00:10:08,800 --> 00:10:11,267
Because I can't remember
anything, not even him.

255
00:10:11,400 --> 00:10:13,433
[MAMENG] Don't worry, dear.

256
00:10:13,567 --> 00:10:16,600
Just rest
and regain your strength.

257
00:10:16,733 --> 00:10:19,567
When your memories come back,

258
00:10:19,700 --> 00:10:20,967
you'll be complete again.

259
00:10:21,100 --> 00:10:22,133
[CHUCKLES SOFTLY]

260
00:10:22,267 --> 00:10:23,933
[UNSETTLING MUSIC CONTINUES]

261
00:10:24,067 --> 00:10:25,067
Hang on.

262
00:10:25,200 --> 00:10:27,400
Didn't you already ask people
to be our lookouts?

263
00:10:27,533 --> 00:10:28,467
Yes, Pa.

264
00:10:28,600 --> 00:10:30,600
We've got people stationed
in the alleys.

265
00:10:30,733 --> 00:10:32,433
If they spot someone unfamiliar,

266
00:10:32,567 --> 00:10:33,800
they'll report right away.

267
00:10:34,500 --> 00:10:36,933
Pa, we need to be cautious.

268
00:10:37,367 --> 00:10:40,233
We can't let Gloria out.

269
00:10:45,200 --> 00:10:50,967
[TENDER MUSIC PLAYING]

270
00:10:51,100 --> 00:10:53,033
[MUSIC BECOMES SILLY]

271
00:10:53,167 --> 00:10:54,867
[SAM]
<i> I've got to hand it to you.</i>

272
00:10:55,333 --> 00:10:57,533
<i> You really care about me.</i>

273
00:11:00,033 --> 00:11:02,000
I thought it was just for show.

274
00:11:02,133 --> 00:11:09,133
[BRIGHT MUSIC PLAYING]

275
00:11:11,667 --> 00:11:13,000
[TOLITS] How much longer
are we going to do this?

276
00:11:13,133 --> 00:11:15,333
We're on watch duty
in the morning.

277
00:11:15,467 --> 00:11:17,233
We're on watch duty
in the evening.

278
00:11:17,367 --> 00:11:18,833
We're on watch duty
the entire day.

279
00:11:18,967 --> 00:11:22,000
I'll start dreaming about
watch duty soon.

280
00:11:22,133 --> 00:11:24,400
Things won't change
even after Gloria leaves.

281
00:11:24,533 --> 00:11:25,600
Tekla was right.

282
00:11:25,733 --> 00:11:28,433
Gloria is a stranger.

283
00:11:28,567 --> 00:11:30,633
She's a YCMA agent.

284
00:11:30,767 --> 00:11:32,533
Her colleagues might
come back for us.

285
00:11:32,667 --> 00:11:34,900
It's not YMCA.

286
00:11:35,033 --> 00:11:36,000
- It's NCIA!
- Ouch!

287
00:11:36,133 --> 00:11:38,400
Know the enemy, dude.

288
00:11:38,533 --> 00:11:39,933
This is only temporary.

289
00:11:40,067 --> 00:11:43,100
We got to help Gabo out.

290
00:11:43,267 --> 00:11:44,133
Hmm?

291
00:11:44,267 --> 00:11:45,167
I've had it with you!

292
00:11:45,300 --> 00:11:46,733
- Hey!
- He's one of us.

293
00:11:46,867 --> 00:11:48,867
- He is?
- I can't get beaten up again.

294
00:11:49,000 --> 00:11:53,033
Why are you drinking
while on duty?!

295
00:11:53,167 --> 00:11:54,933
Have a drink!

296
00:11:56,767 --> 00:11:58,433
Brothers.

297
00:11:58,567 --> 00:12:01,233
[IPE] Did you notice
anything suspicious?

298
00:12:01,367 --> 00:12:04,933
Anyone snooping around
the neighborhood?

299
00:12:05,067 --> 00:12:06,033
Nope, Ipe.

300
00:12:06,167 --> 00:12:07,533
Are you sure?

301
00:12:07,667 --> 00:12:10,133
Not a single person?

302
00:12:10,267 --> 00:12:11,933
No, bro.
It's been quiet here.

303
00:12:12,067 --> 00:12:13,933
We didn't see
anything suspicious.

304
00:12:14,100 --> 00:12:16,300
All right.
But keep your eyes peeled.

305
00:12:16,433 --> 00:12:19,700
If you see anyone
acting suspiciously,

306
00:12:19,833 --> 00:12:21,300
let us know right away.

307
00:12:21,433 --> 00:12:22,467
- Yes.
- All right.

308
00:12:22,600 --> 00:12:24,567
And make sure to be discreet.

309
00:12:24,700 --> 00:12:26,600
Don't blow your cover.

310
00:12:26,733 --> 00:12:27,700
Stay alert.

311
00:12:27,833 --> 00:12:29,167
We got this.

312
00:12:29,300 --> 00:12:31,900
- All right.
- Keep your eyes peeled.

313
00:12:35,600 --> 00:12:36,867
Tuazon.

314
00:12:38,100 --> 00:12:39,667
What really happened?

315
00:12:39,800 --> 00:12:42,933
We were followed
on our way to maximum security.

316
00:12:43,067 --> 00:12:45,333
We were ambushed
near the pier.

317
00:12:47,033 --> 00:12:48,400
What about Team Charlie?

318
00:12:48,567 --> 00:12:52,100
[CASTOR] They covered us, sir.

319
00:12:53,433 --> 00:12:55,200
No one survived.

320
00:12:55,333 --> 00:12:57,300
We were outnumbered, sir.

321
00:12:57,433 --> 00:12:59,933
Good thing NLEA came, sir.

322
00:13:00,067 --> 00:13:04,533
Did you recognize the armed men
you mentioned?

323
00:13:04,667 --> 00:13:06,100
[KAREN] We haven't been able
to identify them.

324
00:13:06,233 --> 00:13:08,333
But if we're talking motive,

325
00:13:08,467 --> 00:13:10,133
they were there
to bust out Victor.

326
00:13:10,267 --> 00:13:12,533
But still, team, good job.

327
00:13:12,667 --> 00:13:15,700
While it is unfortunate
that we lost colleagues again,

328
00:13:15,833 --> 00:13:17,567
despite the attack,

329
00:13:17,700 --> 00:13:22,300
we were still able to transfer
Victor to maximum security.

330
00:13:22,467 --> 00:13:24,233
Good job, team.

331
00:13:24,367 --> 00:13:26,700
You may proceed to debriefing.

332
00:13:26,833 --> 00:13:28,567
- Yes, sir.
- Thank you, sir.

333
00:13:28,700 --> 00:13:32,600
[GRIM MUSIC PLAYING]

334
00:13:32,733 --> 00:13:33,767
Sir.

335
00:13:35,033 --> 00:13:42,000
[GRIM MUSIC CONTINUES]

336
00:13:46,233 --> 00:13:48,333
[MUSIC TURNS TENSE]

337
00:13:57,000 --> 00:14:01,000
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

338
00:14:01,133 --> 00:14:02,867
[TIRES SCREECH]

339
00:14:06,433 --> 00:14:08,433
- Papa! Let me help you.
- Don't touch me!

340
00:14:08,567 --> 00:14:09,967
- [LUCAS GRUNTS]
- Sir!

341
00:14:12,000 --> 00:14:13,533
How could you mess up again,
Lucas?!

342
00:14:13,667 --> 00:14:15,767
We already had Victor!

343
00:14:15,900 --> 00:14:17,367
But they got him back!

344
00:14:17,500 --> 00:14:23,067
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

345
00:14:23,200 --> 00:14:24,967
Tala, get some booze!

346
00:14:27,233 --> 00:14:28,500
Sir, you need a doctor.

347
00:14:28,667 --> 00:14:31,000
No, no, no.
This is nothing.

348
00:14:31,133 --> 00:14:32,233
Hurry up!

349
00:14:35,833 --> 00:14:37,100
[LUCAS] Pa!

350
00:14:37,233 --> 00:14:39,067
I was looking after you!

351
00:14:39,200 --> 00:14:41,133
I had to save you!

352
00:14:44,733 --> 00:14:46,400
I didn't need saving!

353
00:14:46,533 --> 00:14:47,867
I can handle myself!

354
00:14:48,000 --> 00:14:51,333
I've been fighting
long before you were born.

355
00:14:51,467 --> 00:14:54,700
Our mission was to
get Victor back.

356
00:14:54,833 --> 00:14:57,267
And you failed!

357
00:14:57,400 --> 00:14:59,000
What's going on here?

358
00:14:59,133 --> 00:15:02,667
[TENSE MUSIC INTENSIFIES]

359
00:15:02,833 --> 00:15:05,733
[MAMENG] Do the veggies
look familiar to you, dear?

360
00:15:05,867 --> 00:15:06,867
- That's good.
- [SAM CHUCKLES]

361
00:15:07,000 --> 00:15:10,867
Those are the vegetables
they gave you earlier.

362
00:15:11,000 --> 00:15:14,867
And here's the main dish!

363
00:15:15,000 --> 00:15:16,933
<i>- Pagpag!
- [MAMENG CLAPS]</i>

364
00:15:17,067 --> 00:15:19,100
- Wow!
- Yummy!

365
00:15:19,233 --> 00:15:20,933
Woo-hoo!
All right.

366
00:15:21,067 --> 00:15:22,667
- Let's eat.
- [RUDY] Dig in.

367
00:15:22,800 --> 00:15:24,267
- Allow me, Auntie.
- Okay.

368
00:15:24,400 --> 00:15:25,600
- I'll serve my wife.
<i> - Pagpag?</i>

369
00:15:25,733 --> 00:15:27,000
- Yes.
<i> - Pagpag.</i>

370
00:15:27,133 --> 00:15:31,100
It was cooked adobo-style
before being deep-fried.

371
00:15:31,233 --> 00:15:33,033
- Mm-hmm.
- Mm...

372
00:15:34,133 --> 00:15:35,033
Does it smell good?

373
00:15:35,200 --> 00:15:36,733
I can smell the adobo.

374
00:15:36,867 --> 00:15:39,500
- [GABO CHUCKLES]
- How much did it cost?

375
00:15:39,633 --> 00:15:40,633
Uh... It was cheap.

376
00:15:40,767 --> 00:15:43,100
Lato was selling it for 50.

377
00:15:43,233 --> 00:15:44,933
- I offered 40.
- [MAMENG] Really?

378
00:15:45,067 --> 00:15:46,400
- He sold it to me for 40.
- Wow.

379
00:15:46,533 --> 00:15:48,533
- It's that cheap?
- Yeah.

380
00:15:48,667 --> 00:15:53,367
[MAMENG] You see, dear,
<i> pagpag</i> is leftover food

381
00:15:53,500 --> 00:15:55,767
that comes from
different restaurants.

382
00:15:55,900 --> 00:16:00,000
People here collect it.

383
00:16:00,133 --> 00:16:05,200
After they wash it,
they cook it adobo-style.

384
00:16:05,333 --> 00:16:08,567
Then they deep-fry it
to make it extra crispy.

385
00:16:08,733 --> 00:16:12,800
They cook it thoroughly
until you forget it's...

386
00:16:12,933 --> 00:16:14,467
- you know.
- [GABO CHUCKLES]

387
00:16:14,600 --> 00:16:17,733
- That's why it's so good.
- [MAMENG] That's right.

388
00:16:17,867 --> 00:16:19,300
All right, dig in.

389
00:16:19,433 --> 00:16:22,467
You know,
I like the bones most.

390
00:16:22,600 --> 00:16:25,367
- Mm-hmm.
- The flavor's really in there.

391
00:16:26,500 --> 00:16:28,433
- [MAMENG] Dig in.
- Mm-hmm.

392
00:16:28,567 --> 00:16:30,067
[MAMENG] Go ahead.

393
00:16:32,567 --> 00:16:37,200
Gabo, I don't think
she likes the food.

394
00:16:37,333 --> 00:16:38,667
Mameng.

395
00:16:39,533 --> 00:16:42,633
- [MAMENG] Uh...
- Love?

396
00:16:42,800 --> 00:16:44,967
Do you want me
to feed you?

397
00:16:45,100 --> 00:16:48,200
This will taste even better
if I feed her.

398
00:16:48,333 --> 00:16:50,600
- All right.
- [CHUCKLES] Here.

399
00:16:50,733 --> 00:16:52,333
- Okay.
- Love, nibble on this.

400
00:16:52,467 --> 00:16:55,033
All the flavor's in the bones.

401
00:16:55,167 --> 00:16:57,833
[SAM]<i> Lord, what have I
</i> gotten myself into?

402
00:16:57,967 --> 00:17:00,367
<i>Please don't let me
get food poisoning from this.</i>

403
00:17:00,500 --> 00:17:01,800
Go on.

404
00:17:02,733 --> 00:17:05,333
[COMICAL MUSIC PLAYING]

405
00:17:05,467 --> 00:17:06,733
- Ah!
- [MAMENG] There you go.

406
00:17:06,867 --> 00:17:08,900
It's good, right?

407
00:17:09,033 --> 00:17:10,367
Have some rice with it.

408
00:17:11,233 --> 00:17:13,233
- [MAMENG] Oh, dear.
- All right.

409
00:17:13,367 --> 00:17:15,167
- [GABO GIGGLES]
- I'm sorry.

410
00:17:15,333 --> 00:17:18,100
This is the kind of life
we have here.

411
00:17:18,233 --> 00:17:22,967
Our food is simple

412
00:17:23,100 --> 00:17:25,967
but it's delicious, isn't it?

413
00:17:26,100 --> 00:17:27,633
And we're happy here.

414
00:17:27,767 --> 00:17:31,100
The only one
who spoils the fun is Betchay.

415
00:17:31,233 --> 00:17:32,567
Hmm?

416
00:17:32,700 --> 00:17:35,433
The way that woman
treats us is unbelievable.

417
00:17:35,567 --> 00:17:38,400
Just because she's the
only one with a stable job.

418
00:17:38,533 --> 00:17:42,700
So she talks to us
like we're worthless!

419
00:17:44,533 --> 00:17:46,033
What is that?

420
00:17:46,167 --> 00:17:47,267
What the hell?!

421
00:17:47,400 --> 00:17:51,400
The AC is barely
blowing cold air!

422
00:17:51,567 --> 00:17:54,000
- Jeez.
- What's the problem?

423
00:17:54,133 --> 00:17:57,000
- It's working fine!
- [HUFFS] Look at these lights.

424
00:17:57,133 --> 00:18:00,800
They're too bright.
Dim the lights.

425
00:18:00,933 --> 00:18:03,800
We need the lights bright
so they can see our beauty.

426
00:18:03,933 --> 00:18:05,533
- Really? I don't see it.
- Yeah.

427
00:18:05,667 --> 00:18:07,967
Pack on some more makeup.

428
00:18:08,100 --> 00:18:10,633
- Huh?
- This sells better.

429
00:18:10,767 --> 00:18:12,700
- Natural beauty.
- Natural beauty?

430
00:18:12,833 --> 00:18:13,867
- Natural beauty?
- Yes.

431
00:18:14,000 --> 00:18:18,033
Do you see your natural beauty
bringing in customers?

432
00:18:18,167 --> 00:18:21,633
Joyce, have your techy grandson
come over here.

433
00:18:21,800 --> 00:18:22,833
I need him
to do something for me.

434
00:18:22,967 --> 00:18:24,733
- What is it?
- Enough with the questions.

435
00:18:24,867 --> 00:18:27,833
Just have him come here
then I'll explain it.

436
00:18:27,967 --> 00:18:31,567
- Okay.
- You have so many demands!

437
00:18:31,700 --> 00:18:34,933
- What are you trying to prove?
- That I'm a better manager.

438
00:18:35,067 --> 00:18:38,267
Listen up!
I have a plan!

439
00:18:38,400 --> 00:18:42,200
This will make you
look prettier, hopefully.

440
00:18:42,333 --> 00:18:46,667
So more customers
will pick you.

441
00:18:46,800 --> 00:18:48,333
Doll up!

442
00:18:48,467 --> 00:18:50,133
- Call him.
- Okay.

443
00:18:50,267 --> 00:18:51,433
Mm.

444
00:18:52,567 --> 00:18:55,667
What about you, Gabo?
Where do you work?

445
00:18:56,500 --> 00:19:03,467
[CURIOUS MUSIC PLAYING]

446
00:19:05,267 --> 00:19:08,067
Um... I'm...

447
00:19:08,200 --> 00:19:09,600
a messenger!

448
00:19:09,733 --> 00:19:10,600
I'm a messenger.

449
00:19:10,733 --> 00:19:14,500
I deliver things
to different places.

450
00:19:14,633 --> 00:19:19,567
Sometimes I drive for people.

451
00:19:19,700 --> 00:19:20,900
- Mm.
- [GABO CHUCKLES]

452
00:19:21,033 --> 00:19:22,967
Is it a regular job?

453
00:19:24,833 --> 00:19:29,133
I guess so,
but it's not that stable.

454
00:19:29,300 --> 00:19:32,600
But it pays well.

455
00:19:33,700 --> 00:19:35,133
[CHUCKLES]

456
00:19:36,367 --> 00:19:39,033
[SAM] Your job is illegal.

457
00:19:39,167 --> 00:19:42,667
<i> You think I didn't know that?</i>

458
00:19:42,800 --> 00:19:45,533
<i>Did you think
I wouldn't find out?</i>

459
00:19:45,667 --> 00:19:48,067
<i>If I find that
you have a connection</i>

460
00:19:48,200 --> 00:19:50,767
<i>with Mr. Chan
and the Zafras,</i>

461
00:19:50,900 --> 00:19:52,633
<i> I'll arrest you.</i>

462
00:19:52,767 --> 00:19:54,267
<i> I'll take you back to jail</i>

463
00:19:54,400 --> 00:19:57,533
<i>and I can go
back to my old life.</i>

464
00:19:59,000 --> 00:20:01,467
You know, dear,

465
00:20:01,600 --> 00:20:03,900
I hope you don't mind
our humble home.

466
00:20:04,067 --> 00:20:09,133
It may be simple,
but we're very happy here.

467
00:20:09,267 --> 00:20:12,200
We fill it with so much love.

468
00:20:12,333 --> 00:20:13,500
[CHUCKLES SOFTLY]

469
00:20:13,633 --> 00:20:15,467
Except for Betchay.

470
00:20:15,600 --> 00:20:17,233
- Dante!
- [CHUCKLES]

471
00:20:17,367 --> 00:20:20,733
Stop talking about Betchay.
Let's just eat.

472
00:20:20,867 --> 00:20:21,967
[DANTE] Okay.

473
00:20:22,100 --> 00:20:23,333
- Love.
- [MAMENG] Forget her.

474
00:20:23,467 --> 00:20:25,100
- Another bite?
- Yes!

475
00:20:25,233 --> 00:20:27,333
- It's delicious!
- It is.

476
00:20:27,467 --> 00:20:28,767
- Mm.
- Right?

477
00:20:28,900 --> 00:20:30,767
- Mm, delicious!
- One more!

478
00:20:30,900 --> 00:20:33,267
- [CHUCKLES]
- So yummy!

479
00:20:35,000 --> 00:20:36,233
What happened?

480
00:20:36,533 --> 00:20:37,467
[SIGHS DEEPLY]

481
00:20:37,600 --> 00:20:38,833
[DARK MUSIC PLAYING]

482
00:20:38,967 --> 00:20:41,400
[DEBORAH] Don't tell me
you couldn't break him out.

483
00:20:41,533 --> 00:20:43,333
There were two of you!

484
00:20:43,833 --> 00:20:46,200
Blame it on your useless son!

485
00:20:46,333 --> 00:20:48,933
You shouldn't have sent him
with me!

486
00:20:49,067 --> 00:20:50,800
[DEBORAH]
I just wanted to make sure

487
00:20:50,933 --> 00:20:54,100
the plan would be successful!

488
00:20:54,667 --> 00:20:57,400
Pa, I just wanted to make up
for everything.

489
00:20:57,733 --> 00:21:00,167
I had to do something
to save my brother.

490
00:21:00,300 --> 00:21:03,600
All you did was ruin the plan!

491
00:21:03,733 --> 00:21:07,000
Why did you come to rescue me
and not your brother?

492
00:21:07,133 --> 00:21:09,267
Pa, you are more important.

493
00:21:09,767 --> 00:21:11,767
We can still save my brother
another time.

494
00:21:12,567 --> 00:21:16,033
But, you, at that moment,
could have died there.

495
00:21:16,167 --> 00:21:17,233
[DARK MUSIC CONTINUES]

496
00:21:17,367 --> 00:21:18,867
And if we hadn't come,

497
00:21:19,300 --> 00:21:21,333
the NCIA could've eliminated
all of you.

498
00:21:21,600 --> 00:21:23,000
Enough with the excuses!

499
00:21:23,133 --> 00:21:25,533
- [ARTURO] Sir!
- That's enough, Mariano!

500
00:21:25,667 --> 00:21:27,333
Lucas has a point.

501
00:21:27,733 --> 00:21:30,500
If I had to choose
between saving you

502
00:21:30,633 --> 00:21:31,967
and rescuing Victor,

503
00:21:32,100 --> 00:21:33,933
I would do the same.

504
00:21:35,067 --> 00:21:37,567
[MARIANO]
You don't have to save me.

505
00:21:37,967 --> 00:21:39,433
I can handle myself!

506
00:21:39,567 --> 00:21:42,567
Now, because of your meddling...

507
00:21:42,833 --> 00:21:45,633
your brother will rot in prison!

508
00:21:47,833 --> 00:21:48,800
Mariano!

509
00:21:48,933 --> 00:21:52,433
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

510
00:21:52,567 --> 00:21:53,800
[DOUBLE DOOR OPENS]

511
00:21:56,300 --> 00:21:57,300
Boss!

512
00:21:57,667 --> 00:21:58,533
[DEBORAH] Lucas!

513
00:21:58,667 --> 00:21:59,733
- Argh!
- [GUNSHOTS]

514
00:21:59,867 --> 00:22:00,900
Lucas!

515
00:22:01,933 --> 00:22:02,867
[LUCAS SOBS]

516
00:22:03,000 --> 00:22:05,033
- Shh, that's enough!
- Stop this!

517
00:22:05,167 --> 00:22:07,467
- Boss, relax!
- [GRUNTING]

518
00:22:07,600 --> 00:22:09,200
Don't blame yourself!

519
00:22:09,833 --> 00:22:11,233
It's not too late.

520
00:22:11,367 --> 00:22:13,133
We still have a lot of chances.

521
00:22:13,267 --> 00:22:15,600
We can still
get Boss Victor out.

522
00:22:15,767 --> 00:22:16,833
Calm down.

523
00:22:16,967 --> 00:22:19,067
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

524
00:22:19,200 --> 00:22:20,133
There you go!

525
00:22:20,267 --> 00:22:22,200
Are you satisfied
with my grandson's drawings?

526
00:22:22,333 --> 00:22:24,267
These look wonderful!

527
00:22:24,400 --> 00:22:28,733
No wrinkles! Fresh as a daisy!

528
00:22:28,867 --> 00:22:30,900
Such beautiful drawings!

529
00:22:31,033 --> 00:22:32,400
I'm impressed!

530
00:22:32,533 --> 00:22:33,467
[GIGGLES]

531
00:22:33,600 --> 00:22:34,667
My payment, Miss Betchay?

532
00:22:34,800 --> 00:22:36,000
Payment?

533
00:22:36,467 --> 00:22:40,333
You'll be paid from what
your grandma makes tonight.

534
00:22:40,467 --> 00:22:41,700
Oh man, all my efforts wasted...

535
00:22:41,833 --> 00:22:43,600
[BETCHAY] I don't care.
Just go home.

536
00:22:43,733 --> 00:22:45,900
I've got you.
Go on, head home.

537
00:22:46,267 --> 00:22:47,300
What a bummer.

538
00:22:47,433 --> 00:22:49,133
- Go straight home, okay?
- So pretty!

539
00:22:49,300 --> 00:22:51,500
- Look at them!
- What's going on?

540
00:22:51,633 --> 00:22:53,233
- Here.
- Fair-skinned, huh?

541
00:22:53,367 --> 00:22:55,933
- Yeah?
- Wow, just like beauty queens!

542
00:22:56,067 --> 00:22:58,133
- I know, right?
- Looking so young and vibrant!

543
00:22:58,267 --> 00:22:59,567
Totally!

544
00:22:59,700 --> 00:23:00,833
Oh, I know!

545
00:23:00,967 --> 00:23:03,433
- We'll put these up outside,
- Huh?

546
00:23:03,567 --> 00:23:07,033
and they'll catch the attention
of people passing by

547
00:23:07,167 --> 00:23:09,167
and draw them in!

548
00:23:09,300 --> 00:23:11,867
Gorgeous women! Look!

549
00:23:12,000 --> 00:23:13,800
- Well, thanks.
- See that?

550
00:23:13,933 --> 00:23:15,933
- So pretty, right?
- They're perfect.

551
00:23:16,067 --> 00:23:17,100
Wow!

552
00:23:17,233 --> 00:23:19,367
Total manager aura
you've got there!

553
00:23:19,500 --> 00:23:21,000
- [DJANGO CHUCKLES]
- Of course!

554
00:23:21,133 --> 00:23:22,533
Are you looking
for your father?

555
00:23:22,700 --> 00:23:23,533
Nope.

556
00:23:23,667 --> 00:23:24,833
I'm here on business.

557
00:23:24,967 --> 00:23:25,933
My contact will come soon.

558
00:23:26,067 --> 00:23:28,167
Come on, let's grab a table.

559
00:23:28,300 --> 00:23:30,733
Put them up outside, alright?

560
00:23:31,100 --> 00:23:31,933
Follow me.

561
00:23:32,067 --> 00:23:32,933
There, the middle one.

562
00:23:33,067 --> 00:23:34,733
[SILLY MUSIC PLAYING]

563
00:23:34,867 --> 00:23:36,800
- [CHAIR RATTLES]
- [GUN CLATTERS]

564
00:23:37,967 --> 00:23:39,033
Want someone
to keep you company?

565
00:23:39,167 --> 00:23:40,400
[LAUGHS]

566
00:23:40,533 --> 00:23:42,967
The women here are way too old.

567
00:23:43,100 --> 00:23:45,067
- I'm not interested.
- Just kidding.

568
00:23:45,200 --> 00:23:46,400
Don't be mad anymore. Beer?

569
00:23:46,533 --> 00:23:48,233
- Okay, sure.
- He wants a bottle of beer!

570
00:23:48,867 --> 00:23:50,267
Give me one bottle.

571
00:23:50,400 --> 00:23:51,267
[SILLY MUSIC CONTINUES]

572
00:23:51,400 --> 00:23:52,700
Sit down.

573
00:23:52,833 --> 00:23:54,733
Keep me company
while I wait for my contact.

574
00:23:56,700 --> 00:23:57,733
[CHAIR RATTLES]

575
00:23:59,733 --> 00:24:02,500
You've got the same taste
as your father.

576
00:24:05,633 --> 00:24:06,600
You're crazy.

577
00:24:06,733 --> 00:24:07,600
[BOTH LAUGH]

578
00:24:07,733 --> 00:24:08,700
Joke!

579
00:24:08,833 --> 00:24:10,333
[CHUCKLING]

580
00:24:10,467 --> 00:24:11,633
[EXHALES LOUDLY]

581
00:24:11,767 --> 00:24:13,433
These scavenged leftovers
really hit the spot.

582
00:24:13,567 --> 00:24:14,767
I'm stuffed.

583
00:24:14,900 --> 00:24:15,800
[LAUGHTER]

584
00:24:15,933 --> 00:24:17,833
- I'm full, too.
- Gabo...

585
00:24:18,800 --> 00:24:20,367
What's your plan?

586
00:24:20,700 --> 00:24:22,133
You two sticking around
for good?

587
00:24:22,533 --> 00:24:26,900
[PLAYFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

588
00:24:27,033 --> 00:24:28,633
Well, Pa...

589
00:24:28,800 --> 00:24:30,833
That depends on Gloria.

590
00:24:32,033 --> 00:24:33,133
[SAM] Ah, me?

591
00:24:33,267 --> 00:24:34,167
[GABO CHUCKLES]

592
00:24:34,300 --> 00:24:36,600
I can't promise anything.
Because...

593
00:24:36,733 --> 00:24:38,600
I don't remember anything yet.

594
00:24:40,267 --> 00:24:41,133
[GABO] Listen, Pa.

595
00:24:41,267 --> 00:24:42,333
If you ask me,

596
00:24:42,467 --> 00:24:45,100
I'd rather live here
in our house.

597
00:24:45,233 --> 00:24:46,367
Here, we are safe.

598
00:24:46,500 --> 00:24:47,467
Free meals, too.

599
00:24:47,600 --> 00:24:48,667
We've got nothing
to worry about.

600
00:24:48,800 --> 00:24:49,667
[LAUGHTER]

601
00:24:49,800 --> 00:24:50,667
[RUDY] Right, right.

602
00:24:50,800 --> 00:24:52,867
Here? We're not moving out?

603
00:24:53,000 --> 00:24:55,133
[PLAYFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

604
00:24:55,267 --> 00:24:56,300
We're already on our own.

605
00:24:56,433 --> 00:24:57,800
We have our own room.

606
00:25:00,833 --> 00:25:01,667
[CHUCKLES AWKWARDLY]

607
00:25:01,800 --> 00:25:04,500
I thought that
once you get married,

608
00:25:04,667 --> 00:25:08,400
you need to be able
to support your own family.

609
00:25:12,133 --> 00:25:14,967
[SAM] Well, you're jobless.

610
00:25:15,100 --> 00:25:16,267
<i> You're lazy.</i>

611
00:25:16,400 --> 00:25:21,900
<i>You're living off family
and doing shady side hustles.</i>

612
00:25:22,400 --> 00:25:24,567
<i>How will you ever support
a family?</i>

613
00:25:25,700 --> 00:25:27,300
Don't worry, Gloria.

614
00:25:29,600 --> 00:25:31,433
Once we have kids,

615
00:25:31,900 --> 00:25:33,900
I promise that
I'll do everything I can

616
00:25:34,633 --> 00:25:36,033
to give you a better life.

617
00:25:36,200 --> 00:25:38,300
I'm going to work hard.

618
00:25:38,800 --> 00:25:41,500
I'll do whatever it takes
to provide for our family.

619
00:25:41,633 --> 00:25:43,633
I don't care if I go hungry,

620
00:25:44,167 --> 00:25:46,833
as long as I see you well-fed.

621
00:25:46,967 --> 00:25:48,300
[SOFT MUSIC PLAYING]

622
00:25:48,433 --> 00:25:51,167
I'll make sure
you're taken care of.

623
00:25:51,900 --> 00:25:52,967
And all of you...

624
00:25:53,567 --> 00:25:55,133
...will be my greatest love.

625
00:25:58,500 --> 00:26:00,167
[SAM] Did I hear that right?

626
00:26:01,367 --> 00:26:03,200
<i> I can't believe it.</i>

627
00:26:04,000 --> 00:26:05,867
Do people like him really exist?

628
00:26:06,533 --> 00:26:08,267
<i> Someone who'd do anything,</i>

629
00:26:08,400 --> 00:26:09,700
<i> sacrifice everything,</i>

630
00:26:09,867 --> 00:26:11,300
<i> for family?</i>

631
00:26:11,433 --> 00:26:16,200
[SOFT MUSIC CONTINUES]

632
00:26:18,233 --> 00:26:19,233
- Everything's finished.
- Gabo.

633
00:26:19,833 --> 00:26:21,333
Let's go outside for now,

634
00:26:22,133 --> 00:26:24,767
- so Mameng can clean up.
- Okay.

635
00:26:25,767 --> 00:26:27,367
I'll help with the dishes.

636
00:26:27,500 --> 00:26:29,967
N-No, honey, don't.

637
00:26:30,100 --> 00:26:31,167
Auntie, I'll wash these.

638
00:26:31,300 --> 00:26:32,467
I don't want my wife
doing the dishes.

639
00:26:32,600 --> 00:26:36,400
No, I can do it.
Just go with your dad.

640
00:26:36,533 --> 00:26:38,100
- Are you sure?
- Yes.

641
00:26:38,900 --> 00:26:41,100
Auntie, just help her too.

642
00:26:41,233 --> 00:26:42,900
- Sure, sure.
- Let's go. Dante, let's go.

643
00:26:43,067 --> 00:26:44,500
- [DANTE] Alright.
- [CHAIRS SCRAPE]

644
00:26:44,633 --> 00:26:47,167
Mameng can handle this.

645
00:26:47,300 --> 00:26:49,033
- [SAM CHUCKLES]
- [MAMENG] Oh my.

646
00:26:50,233 --> 00:26:51,867
Can you give me that, dear?

647
00:26:54,333 --> 00:26:57,200
Gloria, are you sure
you can do it?

648
00:26:57,733 --> 00:26:59,200
You haven't recovered much.

649
00:26:59,333 --> 00:27:03,567
You might break a plate,
and get yourself hurt.

650
00:27:03,700 --> 00:27:05,367
That's actually better.

651
00:27:05,500 --> 00:27:08,033
That might help me get
my memory back.

652
00:27:08,600 --> 00:27:09,933
Let's help each other, okay?

653
00:27:10,067 --> 00:27:12,400
You wash the plates,
and I'll wash the glasses.

654
00:27:12,533 --> 00:27:13,667
You know, the other day...

655
00:27:14,533 --> 00:27:15,767
Gabo attacked me.

656
00:27:16,533 --> 00:27:19,100
He accused me of shooting Rudy.

657
00:27:19,233 --> 00:27:22,733
- Did you know that?
- That Gabo attacked you? No.

658
00:27:23,567 --> 00:27:26,167
That you're the one
who shot Rudy?

659
00:27:26,300 --> 00:27:27,233
Well, are you?

660
00:27:28,333 --> 00:27:29,700
Hey.

661
00:27:29,833 --> 00:27:31,967
This issue is between Gabo
and me.

662
00:27:32,100 --> 00:27:33,900
I don't involve others
in our mess.

663
00:27:34,500 --> 00:27:35,500
Good for you.

664
00:27:36,733 --> 00:27:37,767
But Gabo...

665
00:27:39,700 --> 00:27:45,167
He'll mess with anyone
and everyone

666
00:27:45,300 --> 00:27:46,833
that he could.

667
00:27:46,967 --> 00:27:48,767
That's why
he has so many enemies!

668
00:27:49,467 --> 00:27:51,633
He has
an extremely bad attitude!

669
00:27:51,767 --> 00:27:53,833
But I heard he earned a lot
of money.

670
00:27:53,967 --> 00:27:55,133
100 hundred thousand pesos.

671
00:27:56,500 --> 00:27:59,000
200 hundred!

672
00:27:59,800 --> 00:28:01,167
Wait, who told you?

673
00:28:01,867 --> 00:28:02,933
Tolits!

674
00:28:04,500 --> 00:28:05,733
What the...

675
00:28:05,867 --> 00:28:10,000
Those men are such gossipers!

676
00:28:10,133 --> 00:28:12,633
[BOTH CHUCKLING]

677
00:28:12,767 --> 00:28:14,300
What's Gabo's secret?

678
00:28:15,400 --> 00:28:16,567
What is his job?

679
00:28:18,000 --> 00:28:19,033
I don't know!

680
00:28:19,733 --> 00:28:21,067
I don't care about him!

681
00:28:21,200 --> 00:28:23,933
What matters is he contributed.

682
00:28:24,100 --> 00:28:25,900
We spent a lot of money
in the hospital.

683
00:28:26,033 --> 00:28:29,467
And he finally helped!

684
00:28:30,100 --> 00:28:31,167
[BETCHAY CHUCKLES]

685
00:28:35,500 --> 00:28:36,633
Gabo.

686
00:28:36,967 --> 00:28:40,167
Is everything you said true?
You know, I'm confused.

687
00:28:40,300 --> 00:28:44,100
I don't know if you're acting,
or your actions are all true.

688
00:28:45,233 --> 00:28:47,633
[DANTE] I completely fell
for your act!

689
00:28:47,767 --> 00:28:52,900
I feel like Gloria
is really your wife!

690
00:28:53,933 --> 00:28:57,233
Let me just remind you, Gabo.

691
00:28:57,900 --> 00:28:59,400
This is all pretend.

692
00:28:59,533 --> 00:29:01,567
Don't catch feelings for her.

693
00:29:02,300 --> 00:29:07,300
If she finds out the truth,
she'll be furious!

694
00:29:07,433 --> 00:29:09,867
She could have you arrested.

695
00:29:10,667 --> 00:29:11,667
But Pa...

696
00:29:14,167 --> 00:29:15,800
I know what I'm doing.

697
00:29:16,467 --> 00:29:18,300
I'm only doing that...

698
00:29:19,133 --> 00:29:21,233
...so we could protect Gloria.

699
00:29:21,367 --> 00:29:24,667
[RUDY] I know,
and I understand you.

700
00:29:25,500 --> 00:29:28,567
I know your intentions are good.
But the problem is...

701
00:29:29,533 --> 00:29:31,333
You might fall for her.

702
00:29:32,300 --> 00:29:33,433
That would hurt!

703
00:29:35,300 --> 00:29:36,700
[DANTE] And Gabo...

704
00:29:36,833 --> 00:29:40,067
If you think you're helping her,
that's good.

705
00:29:40,733 --> 00:29:43,833
But, when you look at it
in the end,

706
00:29:43,967 --> 00:29:45,467
it might turn out to be bad.

707
00:29:46,367 --> 00:29:53,300
["TUNAY NA LIGAYA"
BY JUAN KARLOS PLAYING]

708
00:30:08,367 --> 00:30:13,267
["TUNAY NA LIGAYA" CONTINUES]

709
00:30:13,633 --> 00:30:16,600
If the National Law Enforcement
<i> Agency had not arrived,</i>

710
00:30:16,733 --> 00:30:19,100
<i>Victor Zafra, alias Tiger,
would have escaped.</i>

711
00:30:19,233 --> 00:30:21,800
<i> The NCIA lacked in security,</i>

712
00:30:21,933 --> 00:30:23,900
<i>and we were the ones
who cleaned up after them.</i>

713
00:30:24,033 --> 00:30:26,500
<i>Why are you saying
you saved our operation?</i>

714
00:30:26,633 --> 00:30:29,400
<i>To make
NLEA's public image better?</i>

715
00:30:29,533 --> 00:30:31,933
<i>That NLEA's still
a huge thorn in my side.</i>

716
00:30:32,067 --> 00:30:34,700
And now, they're still blocking
<i> my plans!</i>

717
00:30:34,833 --> 00:30:36,100
<i> We still have Pia.</i>

718
00:30:36,267 --> 00:30:37,900
<i> We already gave you.</i>

719
00:30:38,033 --> 00:30:41,833
Yet my son was still transferred
<i> to maximum security!</i>

720
00:30:41,967 --> 00:30:44,067
<i>Gloria was the first
to help Badong.</i>

721
00:30:44,200 --> 00:30:45,633
<i> If I don't act now...</i>

722
00:30:46,367 --> 00:30:48,133
<i>...it'll be difficult
for me soon.</i>

723
00:30:48,267 --> 00:30:50,700
<i>Gloria's awesome!
You're lucky, Gabo.</i>

724
00:30:50,833 --> 00:30:52,600
<i>It's impossible for Gabo
to have nothing</i>

725
00:30:52,733 --> 00:30:54,267
<i> to tie him to the Zafras.</i>
